  <prompt>
    Author an **optional** `sprk_chartdefinition` config that renders a **count/unread MetricCard** on the record form via the existing VisualHost PCF (`src/client/pcf/VisualHost/`), with **drill-through to Surface 1** (the regarding-mode Timeline / threads view). This is **config-only — NO code**: a Dataverse config record consumed by the shipped VisualHost `ConfigurationLoader.ts` → `ChartRenderer.tsx`, exactly like the existing Matter Health/Budget/Tasks cards (pure config records, no code).

    Requirements (FR-05):
    - **Count-only MetricCard** — the card shows a count (e.g. thread/message count, optionally an unread count) for the record. It MUST NOT render message content, bodies, subjects, sender lists, or any message row.
    - **Drill-through targets Surface 1** — clicking the card drills through to the record's threads view (the regarding-mode Timeline placed by task 022 / the standalone view), via VisualHost's `sprk_drillthroughtarget` → `handleExpandClick` mechanism.
    - **T-1 boundary (MUST NOT).** VisualHost containers fetch **client-side via `context.webAPI` FetchXML**, which honors Dataverse RLS (so private threads are hidden natively) but does NOT honor the `sprk_isinternalonly` internal-only rule that the R1/R2 BFF access filter enforces. Therefore VisualHost MUST be restricted to a **count/summary metric**; **all message content renders via the BFF-backed regarding-mode Timeline (FR-03), never via VisualHost client-fetch** (spec T-1 / NFR-03 / CLAUDE.md MUST-NOT). A count is safe (aggregate, no content leak); content is not.
    - **Optional** — this card is optional (spec Assumptions: "if a count MetricCard is deemed unnecessary at design review it may be dropped without affecting Surface 1"). If dropped, document the rationale; Surface 1 still ships via 020–022.

    Do NOT build a new VisualHost visual type, a thread-preview LIST, or any content-rendering container — that is exactly what T-1 forbids. Config-only, count-only.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Dataverse configuration author fluent in the VisualHost PCF config model (`sprk_chartdefinition` records, `ConfigurationLoader.ts`, `ChartRenderer.tsx`, MetricCard visual type, `sprk_drillthroughtarget`) and the count-vs-content access boundary (T-1: client-fetch honors RLS but not `internal-only`). Familiar with the existing Matter Health/Budget/Tasks config-only cards as the precedent.
  </role>

  <goal>
    An optional `sprk_chartdefinition` config record renders a count/unread MetricCard for a record via the existing VisualHost PCF, with drill-through to Surface 1's threads view. It is config-only (no code, no new visual type) and count-only (no message content) — honoring the T-1 boundary. If the card is dropped at design review, the drop rationale is documented and Surface 1 is unaffected.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      FR-05 offers an optional at-a-glance count card on the record form to complement Surface 1's threads view. The R2 resource investigation (§2) established that a summary count/unread MetricCard is achievable as **config-only** against the shipped VisualHost PCF (config entity `sprk_chartdefinition`; loader `ConfigurationLoader.ts`; dispatcher `ChartRenderer.tsx`; drill-through `sprk_drillthroughtarget` → `handleExpandClick` in `VisualHostRoot.tsx`), exactly as the Matter Health/Budget/Tasks cards are pure config records.

      **T-1 tension (spec §ADR Tensions, path C).** VisualHost containers fetch client-side via `context.webAPI` FetchXML. That honors Dataverse RLS natively (private threads hidden) but does NOT honor `sprk_isinternalonly` — the internal-only rule the BFF access filter enforces on all R1/R2 reads (NFR-03). Rendering message CONTENT via VisualHost would bypass `internal-only`. Resolution (path C — comply): restrict VisualHost to a **count/summary** metric (aggregate, no content leak); render all content via the BFF-backed regarding-mode Timeline (FR-03). This task must stay strictly on the count side of that line. See `docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` (the `Xrm.WebApi` vs BFF boundary) + investigation §2.

      §11 — no new component. This reuses the shipped VisualHost PCF (0 code) via a config record; the investigation explicitly says "Do NOT rebuild a standalone Communications panel PCF — VisualHost provides config/chrome/drill/theme" and "summary count/unread MetricCard = config-only". A thread-preview LIST with drill-through would be a new self-managed visual type — out of scope and, for content, forbidden by T-1. Cost-of-doing-nothing: a nice-to-have at-a-glance metric is absent; Surface 1 still fully ships (hence "optional").
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/pcf/VisualHost/control/services/ConfigurationLoader.ts (READ — how a `sprk_chartdefinition` config is loaded)</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/VisualHost/control/components/ChartRenderer.tsx (READ — visual-type dispatch; MetricCard case)</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/VisualHost/control/ (READ — VisualHostRoot drill-through: `sprk_drillthroughtarget` → `handleExpandClick`)</file>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r2/notes/r2-resource-investigation.md (READ — §2 VisualHost findings + T-1 tension)</file>
      <file>docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md (READ — Xrm.WebApi vs BFF; the count-vs-content boundary)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-05">A `sprk_chartdefinition` config renders a count/unread MetricCard on the record form with drill-through to Surface 1; config-only (no code); count-only. Scope: one optional config record + drill-through wiring.</constraint>
    <constraint source="T-1">MUST NOT render message content via VisualHost client-fetch — VisualHost `context.webAPI` FetchXML honors RLS but NOT `sprk_isinternalonly`. Restrict to a count/summary metric; all content renders via the BFF-backed Timeline (FR-03). Scope: this config record + any drill-through it defines.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03">Access parity — no R2 read surface may bypass the BFF access filter for content. A count aggregate is permitted (no content leak); message bodies/subjects/senders are NOT. Scope: the card's data query stays count-only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Config-only — NO code, no new VisualHost visual type, no thread-preview LIST, no new panel PCF. Reuse the shipped VisualHost (§11). Reference the Matter Health/Budget/Tasks cards as the config precedent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Optional — may be dropped at design review with documented rationale; Surface 1 (020–022) is unaffected either way. No BFF publish-size / CVE obligation (no BFF code; root §10 N/A).</constraint>
  </constraints>

