  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read investigation §2 (VisualHost config model + T-1 tension), `ConfigurationLoader.ts`, `ChartRenderer.tsx` (MetricCard dispatch + drill-through), and `DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` to lock the count-only boundary. Read spec FR-05 + the T-1 ADR-Tensions row.</step>
    <step order="2">Define the count query: a record-scoped aggregate (e.g. count of `sprk_communication` / threads for the record, optionally an unread count) expressed as VisualHost expects (FetchXML aggregate / config fields). Confirm it returns a COUNT only — no content columns (no body/subject/sender rows). RLS hides private threads natively; the internal-only rule does not apply to a pure count.</step>
    <step order="3">Author the `sprk_chartdefinition` config record: MetricCard visual type, the count query, a label, and `sprk_drillthroughtarget` pointing at Surface 1's threads view (the regarding-mode Timeline / standalone view). Mirror the Matter Health/Budget/Tasks config-only records.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify (or plan owner-verify) placement: the VisualHost control hosting this config renders the count card on the record form and the drill-through navigates to the threads view. Confirm NO message content is rendered by the card (T-1). If the card is judged unnecessary at design review, document the drop rationale instead and stop — Surface 1 is unaffected.</step>
    <step order="5">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (023 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (count query used, unread included Y/N, drill-through target, the T-1 count-only confirmation, or the drop rationale if dropped).</step>
  </steps>

