  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A `sprk_chartdefinition` config record renders a count/unread MetricCard on the record form via the shipped VisualHost PCF — config-only, NO code, no new visual type (mirrors the Matter Health/Budget/Tasks cards).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The card is count-only: its query returns an aggregate count (thread/message, optionally unread); it renders NO message content (no bodies, subjects, senders, or rows) — T-1 / NFR-03 honored.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Clicking the card drills through to Surface 1's threads view (the regarding-mode Timeline / standalone view) via `sprk_drillthroughtarget`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No thread-preview LIST, new VisualHost visual type, or new panel PCF was created; the shipped VisualHost is reused unchanged (§11).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If the optional card is dropped at design review, a drop rationale is documented and Surface 1 (tasks 020–022) is unaffected — the acceptance is satisfied either by shipping the count card or by the documented drop.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on task 010 (the count could read via `Xrm.WebApi` directly per VisualHost's client-fetch model; the dependency is on the threads existing + Surface 1 being the drill-through target). Blocks nothing.

    The single hard rule: **count only, never content, via VisualHost** (T-1). VisualHost client-fetch honors RLS but not `sprk_isinternalonly`; a pure count aggregate is safe, message content is not. All content renders through the BFF-backed regarding-mode Timeline (FR-03) which applies the impersonation + 2-rule filter. If any temptation arises to preview thread content in the card, stop — that is exactly the boundary this task exists to hold.

    This card is optional (spec Assumptions). If design review deems it unnecessary, dropping it is an acceptable outcome — Surface 1 ships via 020–022 regardless.
  </notes>

